Optional fields a body written empty would copy into required ones: the
copies are refused (E0343), and the struct holding them is not then
reported as one the target lacks, since the target declares it.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	"crew-roster": {
		owner?: string
		team?:  string
	}
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	"crew-roster": {
		owner: string
		team:  string
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		"crew-roster": {}
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	"crew-roster": {
		owner: string
		team:  string
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0343]: "crew-roster".owner and "crew-roster".team are optional in v0.0 and required in v1.0
  --> history/1.0.thema:11:3
   |
 3 |         owner: string
   |         ----- v1.0 requires "crew-roster".owner
 4 |         team:  string
   |         ---- v1.0 requires "crew-roster".team
...
11 |         "crew-roster": {}
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: write owner: _coalesce(v0_0."crew-roster".owner, <fallback>), team: _coalesce(v0_0."crew-roster".team, <fallback>) in v1_0."crew-roster" to say what to use when they are absent
